'' A MODULE'S ALIAS OVER A GENERIC INSTANCE WHOSE ARGUMENT IS AN ALIAS FROM A FILE THAT SORTS
'' LATER is one type. In 'early', a.tiko's 'T2 as containers.Array( of T1 )' sorts before
'' b.tiko's 'T1 as containers.Array( of ustring )'; DISCOVERY walks the files in that order,
'' so T2 -- and the result type of 'Make( ) as T2', cached on its node -- were resolved over
'' T1's placeholder, and the order-free pre-pass that ran after it fixed the alias alone:
'' 'return x' was TKO0738, "no conversion between these two types". 'late' is the same module
'' in the order that always worked. ModuleTypedefsFirst_ now runs before discovery as well
'' (src/symbols/resolve.bas).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/modules/src/aliasinst/main.bas -o tests/modules/aliasinst.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/modules/aliasinst.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1 1 early
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1 1 late
